L0@P0: 412.541 OPTIONAL PLANS.
L1@P0: Subdivision 1. Optional Plan A. Any statutory city may provide for the appointment of its clerk and
L2@P0: treasurer, or clerk-treasurer and the election of an additional council member as hereinafter provided in this
L3@P0: chapter. These departures from the standard form of government are referred to hereafter as Optional Plan
L4@P0: A.
L5@P0: Subd. 2. Optional Plan B. Any statutory city of more than 1,000 population may provide for the
L6@P0: council-manager plan of government hereinafter provided in this chapter and referred to as Optional Plan
L7@P0: B.
L8@P0: Subd. 3. MS 1965 [Repealed, 1967 c 289 s 18]
L9@P0: Subd. 4. Adoption or abandonment; standard form. Any one of such plans may be adopted or
L10@P0: abandoned in a city by following the proceduresset forth in section 412.551. Until the adoption of an optional
L11@P0: plan, and except as provided in section 412.572, every city shall operate under the standard form of
L12@P0: government earlier provided in this chapter under which the voters elect the treasurer, if there is one, and a
L13@P0: council consisting of a mayor, three or five council members, and the clerk or clerk-treasurer.
L14@P0: History: 1949 c 119 s 66; 1965 c 417 s 6,7; 1967 c 289 s 8,9; 1973 c 123 art 2 s 1 subd 2; 1986 c 444;
L15@P0: 1989 c 30 s 6
